Test SCAN with Ce, symmetry and an input charge-density restart.

The reference includes local XC terms at finite density and zero density
gradient. The previous gradient mask also suppressed these local terms.
Joint charge/kinetic-density mixing (beta=0.3), a real-space charge threshold
of 1e-8, and tighter diagonalization stabilize the XC-sensitive state.
The previous reciprocal-space threshold measured a different residual.
The original 1e-7 eV energy acceptance, restart, cell, pseudopotential, basis
and band count are retained. Independent checks use CG, Davidson and PPCG
at 1/2/4 MPI ranks; Davidson uses pw_diag_ndim=2 in validation copies only.
